{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The mature pine tree is located in the front garden of the property and is clearly visible to road and footpath users, as well as neighbouring properties. The tree is of good form, and contributes significantly to the environmental, ecological, and visual character of the area. Given its condition and prominence, the tree holds high amenity value.",
    "This application has been refused, as it repeats the same request made under applications 12560/TRE/2024/223 and 12560/TRE/2023/304, both of which were previously refused. No new evidence has been submitted to support the claim that the tree is contributing to subsidence. Given the tree's high amenity value, any future application will require robust technical evidence demonstrating a direct causal link between the tree and the alleged damage.",
    "The applicant has the right to appeal this decision to the Planning Inspectorate. Any appeal must be made within 28 days of the date of the decision notice. Further guidance on how to appeal can be fo",
    "The removal of deadwood, dangerous / hanging branches and ivy:  This does not require the formal consent of the Council."
  ],
